                    </li>
                
                    <li data-value="{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fig5&quot;,&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fig5_0&quot;,&quot;imageUris&quot;:[&quot;/view/journals/phoc/55/6/full-JPO-D-24-0098.1-f5.jpg&quot;],&quot;header&quot;:&quot;&lt;sc&gt;Fig&lt;\/sc&gt;. 5.&quot;,&quot;footer&quot;:&quot;&lt;caption encoding-type=\&quot;nlm\&quot; ifp-element-xpath=\&quot;/*[local-name() = 'figure' and namespace-uri() = 'http://www.ifactory.com/press']/*[local-name() = 'caption' and namespace-uri() = 'http://www.ifactory.com/press']\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;(a) Three-dimensional structure of &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; (high-wavenumber slope of the displacement spectrum). The Luzon Strait and the central SCS are marked by black and purple boxes, respectively. (b) Histogram of &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; values in the SCS (blue bars), fitted using a normal distribution (black curve), with labels for the mean value and standard deviation. (c) Histogram of &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; values for the water column of 300\u20132000 m of the global ocean (blue bars), fitted using a &lt;i&gt;t&lt;\/i&gt; location\u2013scale distribution (black curve), with labels for the location parameter, scale parameter, and shape parameter. The global &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; dataset is from &lt;a href=\&quot;#bib45\&quot; id=\&quot;ref_bib45\&quot;&gt;Pollmann (2020&lt;\/a&gt;, &lt;a href=\&quot;#bib46\&quot; id=\&quot;ref_bib46\&quot;&gt;2022&lt;\/a&gt;), which does not distinguish between high- and low-wavenumber slopes, essentially assuming &lt;i&gt;p&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; = &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;.&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;\/caption&gt;&quot;,&quot;altText&quot;:&quot;&lt;caption encoding-type=\&quot;nlm\&quot; ifp-element-xpath=\&quot;/*[local-name() = 'figure' and namespace-uri() = 'http://www.ifactory.com/press']/*[local-name() = 'caption' and namespace-uri() = 'http://www.ifactory.com/press']\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;(a) Three-dimensional structure of &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; (high-wavenumber slope of the displacement spectrum). The Luzon Strait and the central SCS are marked by black and purple boxes, respectively. (b) Histogram of &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; values in the SCS (blue bars), fitted using a normal distribution (black curve), with labels for the mean value and standard deviation. (c) Histogram of &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; values for the water column of 300\u20132000 m of the global ocean (blue bars), fitted using a &lt;i&gt;t&lt;\/i&gt; location\u2013scale distribution (black curve), with labels for the location parameter, scale parameter, and shape parameter. The global &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; dataset is from &lt;a href=\&quot;#bib45\&quot; id=\&quot;ref_bib45\&quot;&gt;Pollmann (2020&lt;\/a&gt;, &lt;a href=\&quot;#bib46\&quot; id=\&quot;ref_bib46\&quot;&gt;2022&lt;\/a&gt;), which does not distinguish between high- and low-wavenumber slopes, essentially assuming &lt;i&gt;p&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt; = &lt;i&gt;q&lt;sub&gt;ξ&lt;\/sub&gt;&lt;\/i&gt;.&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;\/caption&gt;&quot;,&quot;watermarkPath&quot;:&quot;AMS-Logo-Lockup-Journals-01.png&quot;,&quot;currentUri&quot;:&quot;/journals/phoc/55/6/JPO-D-24-0098.1.xml&quot;}]}" aria-selected="false" role="option" data-menu-item="list-id-00266a14-e874-48f6-a03a-7ccb1bf290d7" class="ListItem ListItem--disableGutters ListItem--divider">
                        <div id="fig5-thumb" data-figureid="fig5" class="content-figures-figure figure">
                           <figure>
                               <div class="figure-body flex flex-col flex@xxl-row">
                                   <div style="width: 100%; max-width:300px;" class="figure-image-wrapper w-1 my-auto">
                                       <div style="width: 100%; max-width:300px;" class="image-wrapper flex flex-col flex-align-start">
                                           
                                               <a class="figure-link">
