                        <span class="caption text-caption color-text-primary">
                            <b><sc>Fig</sc>. 10.</b>
                            
<p>Spatial distribution maps of correlation coefficients. (a)–(c) Correlation coefficients of <i>r<sub>E</sub></i> with 〈<i>E</i><sub>sub</sub>〉, 〈<i>E</i><sub>D1</sub>〉, and 〈<i>E</i><sub>D2</sub>〉, respectively. (d)–(f) Correlation coefficients of 〈<i>E</i><sub>NIW</sub>〉 with 〈<i>E</i><sub>sub</sub>〉, 〈<i>E</i><sub>D1</sub>〉, and 〈<i>E</i><sub>D2</sub>〉, respectively. The 〈<i>E</i><sub>sub</sub>〉 is the kinetic energy of subinertial flow. The gray contour represents the 1000-m isobath. The purple box in (d) represents the area analyzed for <a id="ref_fig11" href="#fig11">Fig. 11</a>.</p>
                            
                        </span>


